{"name":"Bering Sea","hex":"#4b596e","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Bering Sea","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The sea between Siberia and Alaska, north of the Pacific Ocean, that is connected to the Arctic Ocean by the Bering Strait."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Bering_Sea"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bering Sea","blocks":[{"text":"The Bering Sea is a marginal sea of the Northern Pacific Ocean. It forms, along with the Bering Strait, the divide between the two largest landmasses on Earth: Eurasia and the Americas. It comprises a deep water basin, which then rises through a narrow slope into the shallower water above the continental shelves. The Bering Sea is named after Vitus Bering, a Danish-born Russian navigator, who, in 1728, was the first European to systematically explore it, sailing from the Pacific Ocean northward to the Arctic Ocean."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/LA2-Bering-Sea-UTM-zones.png/330px-LA2-Bering-Sea-UTM-zones.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bering_Sea","wikidata":"Q44725"},{"title":"Sea","blocks":[{"text":"A sea is a very large body of salty water. The term has two distinct meanings. The first is the interconnected body of seawater that spans most of Earth, known as the sea or the ocean. The second is a named body of water: usually either a marginal sea, or a large, nearly landlocked body of water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg/330px-Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea","wikidata":"Q165"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Beringian_Margin_canyons.png/500px-Beringian_Margin_canyons.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Beringian_Margin_canyons.png/1280px-Beringian_Margin_canyons.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Beringian_Margin_canyons.png/500px-Beringian_Margin_canyons.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bering Sea showing the larger of the submarine canyons that cut the margin","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABeringian_Margin_canyons.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Choris%2C_Saint_Paul.jpg/500px-Choris%2C_Saint_Paul.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Choris%2C_Saint_Paul.jpg/1280px-Choris%2C_Saint_Paul.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Choris%2C_Saint_Paul.jpg/500px-Choris%2C_Saint_Paul.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Russian \"Rurik\" sets anchor near Saint Paul Island in the Bering Sea in order to load food and equipment for the expedition to the Chukchi sea in the north. Drawing by Louis Choris in 1817.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChoris%2C_Saint_Paul.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Noaa-walrus17.jpg/500px-Noaa-walrus17.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Noaa-walrus17.jpg/1280px-Noaa-walrus17.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Noaa-walrus17.jpg/500px-Noaa-walrus17.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Walrus (Odobenus rosmarus divergens), hauled out on Bering Sea ice, Alaska, June 1978. (Source: NOAA)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANoaa-walrus17.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Snailfish.jpg/330px-Snailfish.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Snailfish.jpg/330px-Snailfish.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Snailfish, a non-commercial fish, caught in the eastern Bering Sea","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASnailfish.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Kingcrabpile.jpg/500px-Kingcrabpile.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Kingcrabpile.jpg/500px-Kingcrabpile.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Red king crab","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKingcrabpile.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Aerial_view_of_Tutakoke_Bird_Camp%2C_Coast_of_the_Bering_Sea_just_south_of_Hooper_Bay%2C_Alaska%2C_near_Chevak%2C_Alaska.jpg/500px-Aerial_view_of_Tutakoke_Bird_Camp%2C_Coast_of_the_Bering_Sea_just_south_of_Hooper_Bay%2C_Alaska%2C_near_Chevak%2C_Alaska.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Aerial_view_of_Tutakoke_Bird_Camp%2C_Coast_of_the_Bering_Sea_just_south_of_Hooper_Bay%2C_Alaska%2C_near_Chevak%2C_Alaska.jpg/1280px-Aerial_view_of_Tutakoke_Bird_Camp%2C_Coast_of_the_Bering_Sea_just_south_of_Hooper_Bay%2C_Alaska%2C_near_Chevak%2C_Alaska.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Aerial_view_of_Tutakoke_Bird_Camp%2C_Coast_of_the_Bering_Sea_just_south_of_Hoop